  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\n\nThe monsoon pattern may be done after today, shifting into the\ntransitional season with more frequent troughs. Dry air will \ncontinue to spread across the region through this weekend with \nPWATs forecast to drop below normal, as low as 0.4-0.7\" across the\nlower deserts. The will inhibit any chance at rain. The broad\ntrough moving through the West, helping drive the westerly flow\nand dry air, is expected to shift east into the Plains by the\nstart of next week. Global ensemble guidance then shows an upper\nlow moving out of the Pacific toward the SoCal coast by the end of\nthe day Monday. There is still plenty of uncertainty regarding\nthis low this far out, but it may be what helps eventually drive\nmoisture back up in the deserts and drive the next chance at rain.\nAverage to slightly above average temperatures are forecast this\nweekend through the first half of next week with this forecast,\nwith afternoon highs around to slightly above 100 degrees. With\nthe drier air coming in, the morning lows will finally be more\npleasant, consistently dropping into the 70s for most lower \ndesert locations.",
